id: from-goop
name: From Goop
order: 1
category: body
# "[Majin Regeneration]": it replaces that Primary Racial Trait - which, the table's.
importance: primary
# (2) A Talent of the Minion Category, asked as it is gained - none offered while that Category has none built (Minions wait).
grantsTalentChoiceFrom: minion
description: >
  Made entirely out of a magical, chewing gum-esque substance, you can heal and split yourself into multiple pieces with ease.
text: >
  From Goop (Body) [Majin Regeneration]: Made entirely out of a magical, chewing gum-esque substance, you can heal and split yourself into multiple pieces with ease.
  (1)-[Passive]: You may use your Magic Modifier instead of your Force Modifier when calculating Surgency (see — Surges).
  (2)-[Passive]: Upon gaining access to this Factor Trait, select and gain access to a Talent from the Minion Talent Category while you possess this Factor Trait.
  (3)-[1/Round]: As a Standard Maneuver with an Action Cost of 1 Action and a Ki Point Cost of 4(bT), use a Healing Surge.
  (4)-[Triggered/Threshold]: Use a Healing Surge as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. Increase the amount of Life Points you regain through this effect by 2(bT) for every Health Threshold you are below upon triggering the effect.
  (5)-[Triggered, 3/Round, Ruling]: When you use a Healing Surge, you may halve the amount of Life Points you regain from that Healing Surge to create a ‘Goop’ in an unoccupied Square within a Large Sphere AoE (centered on you), as an Out of Sequence Maneuver. A Goop is a Duplicate Minion, but does not possess the Apparel, Accessories, or Weapons of their creator. A Goop cannot use any Maneuvers except the Movement Maneuver, but they may always take their Act Phase, even if you do not use the Command Maneuver.
  (6)-[1/Round]: As a Standard Maneuver with a Variable Action Cost (1~3 Actions), for each Action spent, Defeat one of your Goops (they cannot trigger a [Triggered/Defeated] effect in response to this effect). If you do, regain Life Points equal to 1/2 of the total amount of Life Points they had remaining. You cannot target a Goop you created this Turn with this effect.
  (7)-[Triggered/Defeated]: You may Defeat any number of your Goops, and regain Life Points equal to 1/2 of the total amount of Life Points amongst all of the Goops Defeated by this effect. Then, use a Healing Surge as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  (8)-[Automatic]: All of your Goops die at the end of the Combat Encounter. Regain Life Points equal to 1/2 of the total Life Points amongst those Goops before they died.

---

# (6), (7)'s Goops and (8): the table's - a Goop is a Minion, and Minions wait (the user's).
[passive]
# (1) The higher of the two, as Majin Regeneration's.
allow surgency.magic;
# (5) Every Healing Surge: asked whether to halve it for a Goop, three times a Round (chat.mjs goopSplit) - the Goop itself, the table's.
allow fromGoop.goop;

# (3) A Maneuver of its own - maneuvers/from-goop-third-effect.dbu, in the list while this is had.

# (4) Knocked through a Health Threshold: chosen on the Threshold's card - 2(bT) Life Points more for each Threshold below.
[triggered/threshold, outOfSequence, effect 4]
surge(healing, 1, 0, 2);

# (7) Reduced to your minimum Life Points: chosen on the Defeated card - the Goops Defeated first, the table's; then the Surge.
[triggered/defeated, outOfSequence, effect 7]
surge(healing);
